{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast","id":806974,"title":"Sell me Beast","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-12T06:50:31-08:00","id":806974,"title":"Sell me Beast","content":"Thread like this popped up in the Changeling forums and it was a joy to read, so I figured I'd post the same sort of idea here because I am on the fence regarding Beast. I read the blurb and it seems pretty awesome but I want to know people's actual experiences the game. I also want to know the places where the game lacks, the houserules that you've incorporated, the stories you've told, your favorite character ideas, etc. I want to know as much about the game as I can before I decide to buy it. So please, sell me on Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T08:42:47-08:00","id":807045,"title":"","content":"Beast is probably OPP's most ambitious Chronicles of Darkness game line as it tries very hard (and mostly succeeds) to position itself as the &quot;cross-over game&quot; line. And the following is a &quot;warts and all&quot; kind of assessment.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately many of its core themes are a bit on the underdeveloped side. Beasts have <i>kinship</i> with some (but not all) supernatural entities but for practical purposes this kinship works best with outcasts from the other splats. It plays with the &quot;I choose my family&quot; theme but doesn't deliver on how that impacts the family left behind (failing to engage with many of the most drama producing themes of commitment and obligation that actual &quot;family&quot; has to deal with). There's also a whole divisive aspect to how the game's fluff evolved over the summer (you can dig those discussion up here and elsewhere -- i.e., the rpg.net forums). There's also the 1 ounce of fat on the 8 ounce steak that takes the form of repeated ephemera rules (from the God-Machine Chronicle) that add nothing to the overall game. That's more of a missed opportunity to flesh out the Hive and Primordial Dream and the entities that populate them than some kind of huge negative.<br /> <br /> As far as I know there's also an extant problem with chapter 6 (being the wrong version?) of the (pre-)production copy being distributed to Kickstarter supporters and via DriveThruRPG. (This may have been resolved or it may be the case that that portion of the text reverted to the original draft. Not sure that anyone at OPP has remarked on that one way or the other -- I might have missed it over the holidays.)<br /> <br /> It is the worst of the 2nd ed game lines produced so far but, you need to take that statement with a grain of salt. While it isn't as good as Demon, Vampire, or Werewolf it is still head and shoulders above most of the 1st edition new world of darkness game lines. And I'm confident that a good storyteller's guide will patch most of the issues because it's primary problem is lack of available word count to fully address the many themes that its ambition demands of itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Outweighing</b> the veritable laundry list of &quot;problems&quot; I've listed, the game provides the very, very large benefit of providing a structured way to run cross-over games. Among other things to consider is the relationship that Beasts have among themselves and among other supernaturals. All in all, Beast presents a very valuable addition to the book shelf of any storyteller whose troupe is interested in cross-over play while also providing many opportunities for its own novel play. (Don't let its imperfections act as a barrier. Consider if it fulfills a role at your table.)<br /> <br /> For my own setting (already heavily crossed-over) Beasts are a highly dynamic population. As predators among themselves, they strive for power. However, since the mechanics tend to level the playing field between high and low powers this means the top dog of a hive is tossed over relatively frequently. Beasts group together in clan-like groupings (not unlike the structures that samurai families built in the 10th to 15th centuries). Those Beasts who interact with the big 4 (Vampires, Werewolves, Mages and Changelings) tend to associate with outcasts (and end up hunted along with them) or end up as &quot;pets&quot; for powerful members of those societies. Those Beasts who interact with the less hegemonic supernaturals (Monsters (aka Prometheans), Revenants (aka Sin-Eaters), Mummies, Demons, and Deviants) have relationships that are more egalitarian. I should mention that this divides the Beast community in my setting between &quot;purists&quot; who only associate with other Beasts and work the top predator of the Hive system and &quot;slummers&quot; who associate with other supernaturals to take advantage of the easy feeding opportunities that Kinship provides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 01-12-2016, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T10:29:25-08:00","id":807132,"title":"","content":"Beast is ambitious in a different way in that the titular characters are predatory, but their predation is enacted without distancing factors. By which I mean Beasts feed (mostly) through human actions and interactions that hurt people just a bit - ways that people are hurt or harassed all the time. Which can be an uncomfortable aspect, leading to the widespread criticism that Beast is a game just about abusing people (which I don't think it is, at least no more so than Vampire). But if you want to explore the dynamics of power, harm, or abuse that lie behind seemingly mundane aspects of life and dark side of humanity stuff, Beast is one of the best vehicles there is.<br /> <br /> At the same time, Beast feeding is incredibly diverse. Each character has a Hunger. One of them is Power: this means the Beast must dominate people to sate themselves. Examples in the game include becoming a corporate shark, lording their way up the hierarchies, making sure every subordinate knows who's boss. Or becoming a judge: it doesn't mean you have to be a hanging judge; the power is the same whether you exercise it fairly or not, and whether the accused is acquitted or not. Or engaging in contest after contest, winning in as many ways as you can. Or being a debating champ (though this example also includes beatdowns of people who respond to losing debates with violence). Or becoming a zealous health inspector, checking every aspect of each restaurant you're assigned to, scrupulously reporting any attempt to bribe or mislead you, and not letting them fob you off even when it might be reasonable. The other four Hungers are just as diverse.<br /> <br /> Consequently, Beast is also a surprisingly good game, despite its outre protagonists, for playing supernaturals who go on living their human lives as much as possible, and interacting with the supernatural world much as mortals do (albeit with more oomph). Which flies in the face of what Jacob said about running very crossover-heavy and supernatural-heavy games, but it can do both (though probably not at the same time).<br /> <br /> As for what you are, you're mostly a human, but instead of your soul, you have a Horror: a monster from a realm of nightmares called the Primordial Dream. The Horror can look like anything you want from the Kraken to Jason - its form is reflected in your choice of Atavisms (one of the main power types, which provide physical powers). It's hungry, and wants to be fed, which is what all the previous paragraphs are about. The more elaborate, specific, or heinous the actions you use to feed, the better the meal for the Horror; you can leave it hungry, but if it's too hungry for too long it goes out into the dreamscape and feeds itself (this mostly means people getting vivid nightmares, but may come with consequences you can't monitor or control). You can fill up, but it's hard to do so while maintaining any semblance of ethics, and if you get <i>too</i> full your Horror gets satisfied and goes to sleep, robbing you of most of your power until you wake it up again. Finding a balance between the metaphysical and moral implications of feeding and hunger - a balance you can live with - is the main psychological question Beasts deal with (their Integrity analogue and fuel stat are the same).<br /> <br /> Another part of you is your Lair. This is a subrealm in the aforementioned Primordial Dream, where your Horror lives. Different parts of your Lair might look like primeval forests, sand-blasted deserts, castles, crushing depths of the ocean, stiflingly hot boiler rooms, libraries filled with books that whisper spidery temptations as you pass, suburban houses that seem relatively normal until you look out of the window, empty streets filled with straggly weeds and the rusted wrecks of cars, and so on. When there's an aspect of the local area that resembles a part of your Lair, you can merge them - which also merges your physical body with that of your Horror. So you can turn into a dragon (if that's what your Horror is), it just needs some prep work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As I said, your Lair is part of you, just as much as your Horror and your human self. You can let people in if you like - you can also let them back out - if you like.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for weaknesses... as I said, it can be an uncomfortable game. I've come across abuse victims who've read the preview who found it almost triggering - and others who found it cathartic. But it is something you're going to have to think about if you emphasise that side of it. I'd also agree that it doesn't have many differentiating themes beyond family, though to me that actually translates into it having different slants on the themes mortals explore, and those of the World of Darkness as a whole. I find it satisfying in that light, anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for house rules. I've not done this in any depth, but the X and Y splats are Family (the flavour of fear your Horror represents), and Hunger. Which seems to me more like two X's - while Hunger can change, it's not common, and not really chosen. So I'd add a philosophical faction too. More or less: Beasts' dreams of their nightmare realm tend to provide them insight, which means leads them to believe their own predations can do the same for humanity (that's in the book); but I'd have a faction that gives that special primacy. One that takes family as the imperative, seeing itself as community builders among other supernaturals. One that gives its human side primacy, living as much of a human life as possible. One that takes its Hunger as the imperative, feeding without guilt or shame (not necessarily without conscience). And probably one that explores the Primordial Dream and its interactions with the Earth beyond their own Lairs and Horrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T10:46:40-08:00","id":807146,"title":"","content":"Holy shit I want to play a Silent Hill inspired version of this game, not sure if my group would be into it as much as me, which is a shame. I'm the horror nerd in the group, they are not so inspired by that sort of thing. Wish I had a webcam and a decent computer so I could play an online game of it.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'll buy the book for my ST and see if he'll run it, he'll be better at it than I will.<br /> <br /> <br /> It sounds incredible, you guys should be getting paid by Onyx Path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T11:05:21-08:00","id":807158,"title":"","content":"I like it more than Promethean. And I f***ing LOVE Promethean.<br /> <br /> I've also found the mechanics to be innovative and evocative, if you like that sort of things <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It also offers such a great freedom in creating characters. Just this afternoon, I wrote down a few notes for an Anakim (Giant) whose Horror is a metal colossus with powerful lights where eyes should be, which stalks places of imprisonment to punish escapees. And even though it was an NPC, I instantly wanted to play her. That's a sign of a good game, to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T11:16:29-08:00","id":807161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=807158#post807158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it more than Promethean. And I f***ing LOVE Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Off-topic, but I hope you like the powers in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T13:22:32-08:00","id":807254,"title":"","content":"The teasing of Transmutations is getting me all excited- count me as another person who loves Promethean. I'm actually playing one in a crossover game right now with a pair of Beasts and a pair of Unchained. It's an interesting group dynamic, and I find as the Promethean that I'm conversely learning a lot and perpetually on edge. Both of the Beasts have Dragonfire as an Atavism. One of them discorporated a GM Angel in two blasts and only suffered a scratch (Hurray for the armour Atavism), so I'm keenly aware that as a Promethean I'm significantly less durable.<br /> <br /> In terms of Beast, the two players of my game are both very, very different characters. One of them took a page from Secret of the Ruined Temple, which discussed the idea of Beasts long before they were Beasts, and has their PC as, essentially, a reincarnation of an utterly ancient Horror who ruled as a Beast Incarnate until they were taken down by a powerful Seer. They intend to purchase Mimr's Well to represent their ancient wealth of knowledge as soon as they can. Her Hunger is for Prey, but it hasn't really come up yet- Family Dinner means she doesn't have to hunt, really. (We also have a Vampire in the party) She plays as sort of an ancient sage, a hunter with a sense of real decorum and honour that would do a Storm Lord proud. The other is an extremely young dragon in comparison (both of the Horrors are dragons) who looks up to the other in utter worship, and has absolutely no problem whatsoever placing herself at the feet of her elder. The character has a Hunger for Ruin, so our first adventure in a piece of GM Infrastructure really got her going. Her player handles the character with a lot of really immense intensity, which kind of makes you forget she's supposed to be this tiny woman and instead constantly treat her the way you'd treat a dangerous animal.<br /> <br /> One of the biggest things I've noticed, playing alongside two Beast characters, is the dissonance between what you see and what is really there. They look like two university age women, but you can just <i>tell </i>something is up. The younger can't help but be constantly predatory, the older is always distant in a way that suggests the weariness of old age until she decides to act, at which point you see that there's still a lot of fire left in her. Atavisms really heighten that dissonance- the neatly manicured hands loping off arms in a single blow is a really jarring image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T16:43:41-08:00","id":807416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lilappleblossom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=807146#post807146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy shit I want to play a Silent Hill inspired version of this game, not sure if my group would be into it as much as me, which is a shame. I'm the horror nerd in the group, they are not so inspired by that sort of thing. Wish I had a webcam and a decent computer so I could play an online game of it.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'll buy the book for my ST and see if he'll run it, he'll be better at it than I will.<br /> <br /> <br /> It sounds incredible, you guys should be getting paid by Onyx Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will say that from what I have read of Beast it's better off as a book for creating powerful well-connected antagonists. As a protagonist though, it seems to me to lacks direction. Albeit, this is all from someone that has yet to play a Beast game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T21:09:24-08:00","id":807583,"title":"","content":"For me Beast offers a really compelling opportunity to play someone trapped in the role of one of humanity's villains, and to determine how they handle that. Unlike most ChoD games Beast doesn't have a mechanical penalty for acting monstrous, no integrity spiral with associated conditions. If anything, the mechanics tend to encourage monstrous behavior. And there are people out there, Heroes, who no matter who you are or how you act, they're going to see a monster and their first instinct is to kill you. So with everyone telling you that you are the monster, you're the villain of the story, do you agree and embrace your role? Or do you fight it? Becoming truly monstrous is in many ways the easy choice, it's how Heroes are going to see you no matter what, and at least this way you get to have fun feeding. But you can also choose to play a Beast who picks the harder path and limits how they feed, searching for low impact or even net positive methods. Your hunger is always going to make it difficult, but you can try to make the world a better place for your presence in the face of those who claim you're everything wrong with it. <br /> <br /> I have a lot of fun devising and playing variations on the second kind of Beast, people who try their best to do good despite a host of incentives to abuse their powers. This is a lot easier if you make friends with other supernaturals. Family Dinner is invaluable for managing hunger, and Beasts have potent mythic abilities that allow them to form symbiotic relationships with most supernats.<br /> <br /> And every once in a while it's fun to play a character with power and no compunctions about how they use it, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T00:34:44-08:00","id":807685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=807161#post807161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Off-topic, but I hope you like the powers in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh man, I can't wait. The 1st ed core book was one of my favorite RPG books of all time.<br /> <br /> Cod 2nd edition as a whole have done a bang up job with making powers fun, useful, and mechanically sound. To get back to the topic at hand, in Beast I love how one can impose their Lair conditions on the environment, provided there's an element of resonance. With all the Traits provided, it opens a wild array of possibilities.<br /> <br /> The ebb and flow of Satiety is great too, because you get more powerful at both ends, but in different ways. Hungry? More powerful Atavisms. Sated? Better Nightmares. So what your character can do is constantly changing, with an element of risk should you go too far either way. It keeps things dynamic and interesting.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T08:13:07-08:00","id":807895,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think at the very least I'll buy the PDF but I will likely never be able to run/play in a game like this. But I just want to read it because it sounds like so much fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T08:18:17-08:00","id":807900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lilappleblossom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=807895#post807895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think at the very least I'll buy the PDF but I will likely never be able to run/play in a game like this. But I just want to read it because it sounds like so much fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast as a whole is very interesting, I would say consider it as a book for antagonists for your games that you run. Beasts have the power to make other supernaturals inherently like them, somehow. This makes them all very well connected as supernaturals are predisposed to like the creature of living nightmares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T09:12:08-08:00","id":807942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=807900#post807900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beast as a whole is very interesting, I would say consider it as a book for antagonists for your games that you run. Beasts have the power to make other supernaturals inherently like them, somehow. This makes them all very well connected as supernaturals are predisposed to like the creature of living nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean &quot;not hate them at first sight, somehow.&quot; Everybody reads Passing Resemblance the wrong way. It's not mind control, it's recognition that they're not necessarily a security risk, and even that goes away if the Beast does something recognisably stupid. Beasts are tolerated because they seem like one of the guys; they're accepted because, in general, they present few of the risks associated with other Supernaturals, let alone mundane humanity (playing politics, arguing over territorial claims, competing for esoteric resources, or going public, to name a few.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T09:14:31-08:00","id":807945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=807942#post807942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean &quot;not hate them at first sight, somehow.&quot; Everybody reads Passing Resemblance the wrong way. It's not mind control, it's recognition that they're not necessarily a security risk, and even that goes away if the Beast does something recognisably stupid. Beasts are tolerated because they seem like one of the guys; they're accepted because, in general, they present few of the risks associated with other Supernaturals, let alone mundane humanity (playing politics, arguing over territorial claims, competing for esoteric resources, or going public, to name a few.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thing is that this is only reflected in beasts, they automagically have a good relationship with other supernaturals. This is not something other supernaturals possess, it is unique to beasts. So while it may be worded in such a way that they seem like &quot;one of the guys&quot; it doesn't rule out that Beasts have the ability to influence the behaviors of other supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T10:18:28-08:00","id":807997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=807945#post807945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is that this is only reflected in beasts, they automagically have a good relationship with other supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they have a stepping stone towards <i>getting</i> one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T12:12:14-08:00","id":808126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=807997#post807997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they have a stepping stone towards <i>getting</i> one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Passing Resemblance isn't some sort of get out of jail free card where all the other supernaturals love Beasts just because. It's a First Impression, not a Friends for Life. All things being equal, that impression won't last if the Beast screws up the social interaction, or is indeed hostile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T12:19:56-08:00","id":808132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=808126#post808126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. Passing Resemblance isn't some sort of get out of jail free card where all the other supernaturals love Beasts just because. It's a First Impression, not a Friends for Life. All things being equal, that impression won't last if the Beast screws up the social interaction, or is indeed hostile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know it's a first impression. But first impressions make up 90% of social interactions. We put a lot of weight on first impressions, so yes it's a very powerful effect because it sets the tone for everything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T13:19:26-08:00","id":808172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=808132#post808132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I know it's a first impression. But first impressions make up 90% of social interactions. We put a lot of weight on first impressions, so yes it's a very powerful effect because it sets the tone for everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're overselling it. Other supernaturals still aren't gonna invite a beast into their parties unless the Begotten proves their loyalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T15:20:55-08:00","id":808274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=808172#post808172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're overselling it. Other supernaturals still aren't gonna invite a beast into their parties unless the Begotten proves their loyalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, getting an invitation to a party is pretty much exactly what you can use a good impression for, without needing to bother jumping the usual hoops or proving loyalty. The minds of other supernaturals just kinda go runny around Beasts, melting into useful shapes willing to do what the Beast wants (within reason), because she's just so strangely likable and vaguely familiar in some undefined positive sense.<br /> <br /> What they can't do right off the bat is IMPERSONATE other supernaturals - that comes a little later, when they've been socializing for a while, and everyone starts forgetting the Beast isn't really one of them - or at least their mind shies away from it as a continual and unbreakable form of influence - and then you can get invited to the really secret parties and join the Lancea et Sanctum r the Autumn Court or whatever. Probably end up in charge, given their raw get-things-done might, which means their friends are in a really good position. But that's the part you need to work at a little. Just being given the location and an invitation to Elysium? You're covered for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","user":"Kingdom of One","date":". 01-13-2016, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T15:32:35-08:00","id":808280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=808274#post808274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The minds of other supernaturals just kinda go runny around Beasts, melting into useful shapes willing to do what the Beast wants (within reason), because she's just so strangely likable and vaguely familiar in some undefined positive sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be fantastic if we could refrain from framing the supernatural equivalent of wearing the right outfit as though it were outright mind-control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T15:57:50-08:00","id":808300,"title":"","content":"Seriously people, look at the social maneuvering rules, what a good impression actually does, and the suggestions for how a mortal can gain one. It's something you can get with a good outfit and a firm handshake, no supernatural powers required. Defaulting to a good impression is less mechanically impressive than Striking Looks, a 1 dot merit available to literally everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T05:53:23-08:00","id":808603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=808280#post808280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be fantastic if we could refrain from framing the supernatural equivalent of wearing the right outfit as though it were outright mind-control.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know why it'd be fantastic. The description explicitly says it's not mind control, but it's also clearly supernatural. It's like a solid half-page of text just to explain how it works, which is a little above and beyond the mundane nature of the Impression system. If it were &quot;the right outfit&quot; then the entire section would be pointless because there's already rules for that kind of thing and you could just refer back to them, instead of going into detail about the ways others just naturally find themselves bending to your smile. Something about you disarms the natural fear and distrust other predators have of things that stalk in the dark alongside them, because &quot;I seek out and hurt people for fundamentally inhuman reasons&quot; is usually not enough of a shared middle ground to get around to appreciating each other's fashion sense. Note that the still-human types <i>don't </i>get a good impression.<br /> <br /> All else equal, the Beast gets a good impression where someone else wouldn't get anything. It doesn't climb in the back of a vampire's head and tell him you're his new best buddy, but it does put aside years or decades or centuries of monster instincts to give you a chance <i>you wouldn't ordinarily get</i>. That's magic, not a suit and tie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T06:06:02-08:00","id":808611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All else equal, the Beast gets a good impression where someone else wouldn't get anything. It doesn't climb in the back of a vampire's head and tell him you're his new best buddy, but it does put aside years or decades or centuries of monster instincts to give you a chance <i>you wouldn't ordinarily get</i>. That's magic, not a suit and tie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but it's mechanically equivalent to &quot;If the persuading character influences the interaction - wearing appealing clothes, playing appropriate music, or meeting in a pleasant environment - that moves up to a good impression [from average].&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah, literally the supernatural equivalent of wearing a nice suit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T06:42:44-08:00","id":808635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=808611#post808611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, but it's mechanically equivalent to &quot;If the persuading character influences the interaction - wearing appealing clothes, playing appropriate music, or meeting in a pleasant environment - that moves up to a good impression [from average].&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah, literally the supernatural equivalent of wearing a nice suit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because it's very limited form of mind-control it still is mind control. That's like saying just because it's not DOMINATE PERSON it's no concern, because it's only Charm Person. Heck, little alterations like these are what Mind 3 can do &quot;The minds of other\u2019s may be manipulated to allow the mage to appear as someone one isn\u2019t.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T07:03:23-08:00","id":808651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=808635#post808635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just because it's very limited form of mind-control it still is mind control. That's like saying just because it's not DOMINATE PERSON it's no concern, because it's only Charm Person. Heck, little alterations like these are what Mind 3 can do &amp;quot;The minds of other\u2019s may be manipulated to allow the mage to appear as someone one isn\u2019t.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because otherwise it would work in all situations, not just &quot;all else being equal&quot;. As it stands, any time a Begotten introduces themselves impolitely, disrespectfully, or in a hostile manner, Family Resemblance won't help, and in all future interactions it won't have any effect.<br /> <br /> Claiming that it's mind control is as inaccurate as it is intentionally misleading in an attempt to convince people that beasts are somehow overpowered or Mary Sues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T07:07:18-08:00","id":808653,"title":"","content":"Majesty 1 does nothing more than remove penalties and give a social bonus - that's the equivalent of having the right equipment. And its clearly mind control. I think its more that people have an extreme reaction to anything that might hint at taking away player agency. Social mechanics have always been touchy in a way investigations, chases, and combat have never been, because some people feel that social-fu is taking away player agency. &quot;You can't tell me what to do! You can't make me like you!&quot;<br /> <br /> I think its more of a knee jerk reaction against any kind of social-interaction mechanics and calling it mind control to be dismissive of it, because how dare we have our stone cold killer-person be so easily swayed! This, coupled with misunderstandings of how Social Maneuvering / interaction works, is the heart of the issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=808274#post808274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, getting an invitation to a party is pretty much exactly what you can use a good impression for, without needing to bother jumping the usual hoops or proving loyalty.</div> </div> </div> </div> Except not. Social maneuvering won't make some people cross hard lines. One of the first things explicitly stated. Bringing an unknown stranger to a party crosses a lot of lines in supernatural society. Like, potentially lethal consequences. That's going to require more than being a super charming person. Furthermore, some stranger coming up and asking to get into a party right off the bat falls into &quot;that circumstances modify the impression level for the Beast, even taking Thicker Than Water into account.&quot; <br /> <br /> Social maneuvering has three results - either you go along with whatever the person wants and get a beat, you propose an alternative and gain a Condition, or outright refuse because it crosses a hard line. There's subtlty, flexibility and discretion involved here, as well as some limits.<br /> <br /> Here's also a funny thing - &quot;proving loyalty&quot; is possible as a way to open doors. Here's another funny thing. Beasts use Nightmares to force doors as Hard Leverage. Social interaction with Beasts carries an edge of fear with them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What they can't do right off the bat is IMPERSONATE other supernaturals </div> </div> </div> Unless they've bonded with someone else before. You can be a stranger to one vamp but Kin to a second in another city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-14-2016, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T07:08:29-08:00","id":808656,"title":"","content":"The Beast doesn't appear as someone they aren't. They don't become any different to the other party. There just happens to be something familiar about the Begotten as a matter of their nature, some inherent feeling of supernatural kinship that in neutral circumstances has the advantage of smoothing over interactions with other monsters.<br /> <br /> It's no more mind control than treating someone with an open mind or the benefit of the doubt on your first meeting because they have a similar feeling to a family member or remind you of a friend in the way they are or carry themselves.<br /> <br /> And some people are distrustful of those natural impressions or make an effort to not be affected if they consciously recognize it. Some supernaturals will have more reasons to be distrustful of such a thing and will act accordingly, evening out the mechanical benefit or turning it negative. But that doesn't make it mind control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 01-14-2016, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T07:27:05-08:00","id":808673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=808635#post808635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because it's very limited form of mind-control it still is mind control.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm kind of curious where the &quot;control&quot; part of all of this is coming into play. Because it sounds like people are assuming that social maneuvering = mind control. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T08:33:39-08:00","id":808728,"title":"","content":"&quot;Subliminal nudging that Beasts might not even be fully aware of&quot; seems a more accurate term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:26:38-08:00","id":808812,"title":"","content":"I'm not trying to be punny, it just seriously seems like people have never met people with natural animal magnetism before. Beasts have it for supernaturals, that's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:27:49-08:00","id":808815,"title":"","content":"Also, Reshy, you don't like Beast-what the hell are you doing in a thread <i>trying to sell it</i>?<br /> <br /> I mean, there's acknowledgment for flaws, and then there's asking the haters for their opinions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:04:12-08:00","id":808859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=808815#post808815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Reshy, you don't like Beast-what the hell are you doing in a thread <i>trying to sell it</i>?<br /> <br /> I mean, there's acknowledgment for flaws, and then there's asking the haters for their opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because presumably the OP wants to know it's flaws as well as its strengths. Should we just ignore negative reviews of a product?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:07:23-08:00","id":808863,"title":"","content":"Yes, but we should probably stick to flaws that actually exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:16:53-08:00","id":808874,"title":"","content":"Easy lads and ladies, all in good fun. I don't want this to end up in a fight. I have read every post and taken into account everyone's words and I thank everyone for the opinions, negative or otherwise. I'm excited to buy the book and have some fun with it, even if it's just for flavor in my other games. I'm already writing up a story for a character that I'd love to play, we'll see if she ever sees the light of day. But regardless you guys are awesome for spending your time educating me on the pros and cons of the game. I greatly appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T14:06:21-08:00","id":809071,"title":"","content":"What I find especially weird about people worrying about Thicker than Water is that Beasts do have some crazy powerful social abilities. With Siren's Treacherous Song, Alien Allure, and Advanced Striking looks it's very easy to make a Beast who does have social dice that practically equal mind control powers.<br /> <br /> Thicker than Water is nowhere near that level of utility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T16:42:28-08:00","id":809204,"title":"","content":"Actual mind control is playing fair. They don't like Thicker than Water because they just read it as &quot;everyone likes beasts for no reason&quot; (because apparently they need their eyeballs replacing or something) and that sounds a bit mary-sueish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T16:48:40-08:00","id":809210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=809204#post809204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actual mind control is playing fair. They don't like Thicker than Water because they just read it as &quot;everyone likes beasts for no reason&quot; (because apparently they need their eyeballs replacing or something) and that sounds a bit mary-sueish.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/9hC7N.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">reading about the Kender from Dragonlance</a>. How despite being a race of thieving pickpockets everyone's predisposed to like them. Only in this case it's a race of loving nightmares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 01-14-2016, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T17:03:45-08:00","id":809223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=809210#post809210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's like <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/9hC7N.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">reading about the Kender from Dragonlance</a>. How despite being a race of thieving pickpockets everyone's predisposed to like them. Only in this case it's a race of loving nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a race of incarnate terrors from the base supernatural lizard-brain whose main powers work on the basis of like-calls-to-like. Monsters attract monsters, particularly compatible ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T18:22:57-08:00","id":809281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=809071#post809071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I find especially weird about people worrying about Thicker than Water is that Beasts do have some crazy powerful social abilities. With Siren's Treacherous Song, Alien Allure, and Advanced Striking looks it's very easy to make a Beast who does have social dice that practically equal mind control powers.</div> </div> </div> </div> The only thing approaching mind control is the Alien Allure ability to put Charmed on someone after removing Doors. Every thing else you listed? Meh. Pretty worthless. <br /> <br /> Here's the thing about Social Maneuvering. Your dice pool size doesn't really matter that much. Unlike combat, there's absolutely no difference between one success and four; if you can reliably get an exceptional success, you remove 2 doors instead of 1! So, shy of maxing out one dice pool for that, the dice pool is pretty meaningless. Siren's Song, Alien Allure, and ASL can reliably get you that exceptional success for one extra Door. Which... is dull compared to the fact that the very next merit, Sympathetic, can open two doors at once, at a cheaper cost than ASL, and gives you a Condition that will give you more beats. <br /> <br /> You want to know how to really max out social-fu for a Beast? Look for abilities that either improve your Impression, or directly opens Doors. Use Nightmares as Hard Leverage, and combine that with Looming Presence. Regular use of Nightmare is one door. High Satiety is two doors. Spend a point of Satiety for three doors. Looming Presence (normal version) boosts that to four doors open. Combine with Sympathetic for six doors. Make a regular roll beforehand for an aditional door. We're up to seven doors with only needing one success, and two powers. The maximum number of doors, shy of someone with Resolve AND Composure 6+, is 9, and that's really extreme situations. Then, lets add on the Fast Talking merit. Very first dot reduces the target's effective Resolve and Composure when calculating Doors, effectivley removing one. Fourth dot opens an additional doors whenever you make a roll. Right there. Open 9 Doors, the effective maximum, at once. There are ways to boost that even higher. <br /> <br /> Alien Allure and Siren's Treacherous Song do help, but, once again interestingly, the best benefits are actually at Normal instead of Low Satiety or Satiety Expendature. No, not the boost to dice pools. Its the &quot;always reset to Good Impression&quot; and &quot;Counts as a Vice.&quot; Combined, the two let you raise your Impression to Exceptional, open an additional Door with Fast Talking 5 AND you can use Hard Leverage with vritually no ill effect (resets to Good). <br /> <br /> Low Satiety Alien allure is overrated. While the Charmed condition <i>sounds </i>attractive, its not really that big of a deal. You're better at lying with the target, and you can ask favors. Low Satiety Sirens already have a big boost to lying, making it a bit redundant, and you've already got the target to do you favors because you jsut finished Social Maneuvering him. In theory, a Charmed target never needs to be Maneuvered again, but its only a few rolls to get more favors as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T21:33:30-08:00","id":809364,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that if you choose to force doors in a single roll, every door is a -1 penalty. Enough bonus dice allows you to ignore the social maneuvering system entirely and just force doors. A lair 1 Beast with Siren's Treacherous Song, Alien Allure and Advanced Striking looks is at +4 (effectively canceling 4 doors) and *rote*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T03:05:44-08:00","id":809467,"title":"","content":"Forcing doors is part of the social maneuvering system. There are still the same limits in place. So it doesn't let you ignore it, just use a single tactic that is actually still easier to pull off with just Nightmares - remember that Forcing Doors requires Hard Leverage, and Nightmare usage is untraceable, unlike a gun. And Allien allure Low Satiety requires no Hard Leverage to be of any use; actually, on the matter, Alien Allure and Siren's Treacherous Tongue are designed to be used with subtle persuasion, not threats. If you take ASL with intimidating, you can't use it for persuasion either, so that's less than helpful too.<br /> <br /> Or, hell's bells, just use You Must Obey. THAT is the ultimate in hard leverage control for a Beast. And actually does bypass the social manuevering system.<br /> <br /> Vampires, when they want to get their way, use Dominate or other Disciplines to bypass the social system, or the Vinculum. Werewolves (notably Irraka for subterfuge and cahalith for persuasion) have auspice abilities, Dominance Gifts, and Inspiration Gifts for manuevers; instant Perfect Impression means dice pool size doesn't matter, and there are several ways that wolves negate the penalties for Hard Leverage. Mages will get spells that open all Doors instantly.<br /> <br /> Dice pool size for Hard Leverage tends to come into play for rank mortals, who lack magical bonuses for these skills anyways. And, even then, mortal hard leverage &quot;benefits&quot; from making difficult Integrity checks for auto-removing more doors without the dice pool penalty. But supernaturals have better means of either avoiding or using social maneuvering system that doesn't rely on high dice pools.<br /> <br /> The way successes work in the CofD is different from before. In the past (ie in 1e), you wanted giant dice pools to leverage your way. Now, not as much. Combat looks to see who has the better equipement for auto-successes / armor negating successes; there are some situations where slightly higher dice pools carry an edge, but its not as striking as it was before. Social maneuevers wants Impressions and Auto-remove doors. Investigation cares only about single successes when rolled. The number of dots do matter here, but not because you roll them, but because you get better clues if you're an &quot;expert&quot; (4 dots in a skill, attribute could be a 1 and still get that bonus). Hells, exceptional success just gives you a Condition, and not better clues.<br /> <br /> <br /> Generally speaking, almost any roll is determined by success/failure, and doesn't care about how many of those successes you roll. Sure, you're better off wtih exceptional successes if you can reliably pull it off, but its not as critical as you'd think - investing in supporting merits tends to produce better results. Yes, you want a sizable enough dice pool to deal with any negative modifiers and still reliably get a single success, but equipment also helps there.<br /> <br /> Chases, combat, and research rolls are areas where the number of successes matter. In chases, though, maxing out your speed and initiative give you more of an edge than pure dice, since it modifies what the opponent needs. Combat still cares, but less important outside of grappling than auto-scucesses from weapons / vigor equivalents.<br /> <br /> There are two situations where you do want absolutely to focus on maxed out dice pools over other options. One is extended rolls - usually research (generally for finding Banes/Bans, otherwise we seem to be defaulting to Investigation rules instead), and extended action magics like blood sorcery and wolf rites. The other is any situation where you're in a contested action against someone else. Clash of Wills is probably the most famous of contested rolls, followed by grappling. Almost everything else seems to use special systems that operate on dramatic/failure/success/exceptional- including contested tracking; yes, werewolf tracking doesn't seem to benefit overmuch from large dice pools either except to get exceptional successes. These are also the only systems that let you max out a single dice pool - chases and combat are fluid enough that chances are your dice pool is going to be moved around a lot. When something as crazy as Wits+Crafts is a valid dice pool for a chase, you're better off off focusing on being a generalist than a specialist. Extended rolls with single dice pools let you get away with being a one trick pony, and contested actions can sometimes be an issue. Nothing else does, and, in fact, often penalizes you for using the same dice pool over and over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-15-2016, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T04:07:09-08:00","id":809487,"title":"","content":"I have found ten minutes of Internet connection on a prehistoric computer in my public library so I can drop my personal experience around.<br /> <br /> I ran a brief game of Beast. Now then, I absolutely love the game, probably my favorite of the CoD, I wrote TONS of content for it, but have not much time so I'm not going to give you my own opinions because I recognize they may be biased. Just gonna share my table experience.<br /> <br /> Based on what happened in my games, Thicker than Water did not proved that useful much often, Aside from one of my players, the others had no interest socializing with other non-Beast monsters and they usually made no use of that &quot;good first impression&quot; we're talking about here. Truth be told, they usually burnt it very quickly or made their first approach with other supernaturals with it already compromized. No amount of Thicker than Water is going to convince a vampire you're a nice fella when it's well known that you're the one who dealt with another group of vampires by closing them into a container and melting it with your Dragonfire in order to give a message to all the bloodsuckers of the city. I have other examples who are less blatant, but you get the idea.<br /> <br /> It's really not a big deal when you run it as intended and written","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-15-2016, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T05:14:04-08:00","id":809514,"title":"","content":"Forcing Doors does not require Hard Leverage, I don't know where you're getting that from but it's definitely not in the text. Forcing doors is a single contested roll, with remaining doors acting as a penalty on your roll. When forcing doors you either open all of the doors if you win the roll, or lose all chance to try again if you lose. It is exactly where you need a huge social pool, because you're rolling against the other character's pool at a penalty.<br /> <br /> Here's the entire text: <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">Sometimes, waiting and subtlety just aren\u2019t warranted, desired, or possible. In these cases, your character can at- tempt to force a character\u2019s Doors. This degree of urgency is high-risk, high-reward. Forcing Doors often leads to burnt bridges and missed opportunities. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">When forcing Doors, state your character\u2019s goal and her approach, then roll immediately. The current number of Doors apply as a penalty to the dice roll. The subject contests as normal. If successful, proceed to resolution as normal. If the roll fails, the subject is immune to further efforts at social maneuvering from your character. </span><br /> <br /> Hard Leverage is not required, proceed to resolution on a success, bypassing all remaining doors. It says you aren't being subtle but that doesn't equate to threats, it can also be straight up asking for what you want without trying to warm the person up first. STS adds Lair, AA adds Lair again, ASL adds +2 and Rote. Even at Lair one you can reliably force doors against weaker willed characters, and once you get to higher Lair the dice bonus becomes so large that resistance is largely irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T06:29:11-08:00","id":809544,"title":"","content":"Hard Leverage that causes Integrity loss is not required, and Forcing doors is the only time you can use it. <br /> <br /> But here is the thing. Hard Leverage refers to intimidation/blackmail/etc that inflicts Integrity equivalent risks. You still need some kind of approach that is forceful and still reasonable. If its not reasonable or realistic, the ST will say no. Walking up to a Congressman and demanding he vote no on a bill his lobbyists want? That is not reasonable, no matter how many dice you have. <br /> <br /> You can't Force Doors by being nice. Being upfront and asking nicely won't cut it. Forcing Doors, by name, implies that we are not respecting boundries. We are engaging in actions that can burn bridges. Upfront demanding without some kind of persuasive forceis exactly the kind of case covered by &quot;the ST determines if the request is reasonable&quot; clause in the very beginning of the section. <br /> <br /> You need to do -something- that will potentially cause them to never trust you again. Otherwise, its not forcing anything. Its merely another attempt at normal persuasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T14:32:37-08:00","id":809843,"title":"","content":"I never really noticed, but Hard Leverage is basically removing -1 or -2 in penalty for your roll in exchange for an Integrity check of some kind, which is normally not a great deal even if you're really desperate. Huh. I think the idea of removing Doors sounded great and I assumed you could include that into normal social maneuvering, but if you're forcing anyway - and forcing is easier than I remembered as well - I don't see why you would, except for gravitas, or if there's some effect at play that further complicates the issue.<br /> <br /> Speaking of further complication, so can Beasts not use Hard Leverage at all? They can't make breaking point rolls, right? It doesn't actually ever bother them to inflict atrocities on human beings, there's no point at which they are psychologically compelled to say &quot;when,&quot; and so there's nothing they can do to push themselves into the kind of uniquely human desperation needed to deliberately betray your own principles just to prove a point.<br /> <br /> The &quot;no breaking points&quot; thing seems like a...mixed bag potential sell, in relevance to the thread topic. On the one hand, you can literally do anything and it won't drive you insane, toss schoolbuses over ravines, re-enact all the cooking scenes from the Hannibal TV series, not pay for WinRAR even after the free trial period has expired, whatever fiendish machinations you can imagine are yours to vicariously live out through your unstoppable mythic god-monster. On the other hand, I bet Hard Leverage isn't the only wonky interaction that comes from being actually unable to suffer breaking points. Also you probably have to socialize with people who also have absolute freedom from psychospiritual accountability or whatever exactly you consider Integrity to be, so if you have a button there's a chance the horror next door gets a kick out of pushing it. (Although you CAN just eat them)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","user":"Kingdom of One","date":". 01-15-2016, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T16:46:02-08:00","id":809920,"title":"","content":"The breaking point thing is just a metric to determine how effective it is. The guy whose hand you're smashing with a hammer isn't going to be any less coerced to do what you want just because you don't give a shit about it. That would be silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T23:25:23-08:00","id":810504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=809920#post809920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The breaking point thing is just a metric to determine how effective it is. The guy whose hand you're smashing with a hammer isn't going to be any less coerced to do what you want just because you don't give a shit about it. That would be silly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was going to say that if it's silly, then Hard Leverage is silly, because that's exactly how it works, but now I'm not sure. You need to risk a breaking point, on that it's clear, but the modifier is checked &quot;not considering the character's breaking points.&quot;<br /> <br /> Immediately afterwards, the example notes the importance that the action would be a breaking point for the character. And, in fact, takes into account her specific breaking points. But that's what you should ignore? Maybe? Now I'm just confused.<br /> <br /> So I think it has to actually cause you to roll for a breaking point but your particular psychology is irrelevant, maybe? So that still excludes Beasts. My concept of Hard Leverage isn't &quot;smashing hands is scary&quot; because I put that as a situational modifier to the Intimidation roll. My concept of Hard Leverage is &quot;I'm acting on pure desperation,&quot; determined by the sin you're willing to commit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","user":"Kingdom of One","date":". 01-17-2016, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T04:51:45-08:00","id":810573,"title":"","content":"Having it be based on the character's own integrity means that you could have two otherwise-identical characters doing the exact same thing to the exact same person, but one of them would succeed in convincing their victim while the other would not. This makes absolutely no sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T05:27:18-08:00","id":810582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=810504#post810504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was going to say that if it's silly, then Hard Leverage is silly, because that's exactly how it works, but now I'm not sure. You need to risk a breaking point, on that it's clear, but the modifier is checked &quot;not considering the character's breaking points.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I just read that entire section as... &quot;Look at the table on page 73 for guidance on how extreme the actions need to be in order to count as Hard Leverage and for more extreme actions you get another door for free, because we'd love to go into it here but we only have a couple of pages to explain this brand new system and by using the same table twice I get an extra half a page to add in examples.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also I think that the purpose of that phrase &quot;not considering the character's breaking points&quot; is pretty clearly intended to represent that this is the general modifier suggested for everyone, rather than the individual one for that particular character, which indirectly implies that it's not based upon the threatening party's own moral code or integrity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T08:14:35-08:00","id":810631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=810573#post810573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having it be based on the character's own integrity means that you could have two otherwise-identical characters doing the exact same thing to the exact same person, but one of them would succeed in convincing their victim while the other would not. This makes absolutely no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would have hoped you could make sense from my last post, but again: <i>it has nothing to do with the action</i>. It's like spending a Willpower point and one of you succeeds and one of you fails. The difference is an internal process. Hard Leverage is about self-compromise, and it's effective for the same reason pushing yourself to the limit and spending Willpower is effective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I just read that entire section as... &quot;Look at the table on page 73</div> </div> </div> </div>It's explicitly not the intent unless the Example section had a different writer who wasn't paying attention. More, it wouldn't have been hard to say &quot;an action that comprises a breaking point&quot; or something, but it doesn't. It says <i>the character suffers</i> a breaking point. That's significant, and the example bears it out, since it references, again, the character's own breaking points and internal response not just as &quot;you happen to suffer a breaking point&quot; but to determine the actual leverage involved. The line about ignoring your breaking points is in direct contradiction with both rules and example text.<br /> <br /> It doesn't make sense. Either reading, there's a paradox. No reading resolves it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T09:42:50-08:00","id":810663,"title":"","content":"Spending willpower is not entirely internal. It represents the character pushing themselves in a time of crisis, and therefore represents them doing something slightly different to someone who didn't spend it. You can't do extra damage to someone just by wishing hard enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T12:54:33-08:00","id":810760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=809843#post809843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never really noticed, but Hard Leverage is basically removing -1 or -2 in penalty for your roll in exchange for an Integrity check of some kind, which is normally not a great deal even if you're really desperate. Huh. I think the idea of removing Doors sounded great and I assumed you could include that into normal social maneuvering, but if you're forcing anyway - and forcing is easier than I remembered as well - I don't see why you would, except for gravitas, or if there's some effect at play that further complicates the issue.<br /> <br /> Speaking of further complication, so can Beasts not use Hard Leverage at all? They can't make breaking point rolls, right? It doesn't actually ever bother them to inflict atrocities on human beings, there's no point at which they are psychologically compelled to say &quot;when,&quot; and so there's nothing they can do to push themselves into the kind of uniquely human desperation needed to deliberately betray your own principles just to prove a point.<br /> <br /> The &quot;no breaking points&quot; thing seems like a...mixed bag potential sell, in relevance to the thread topic. On the one hand, you can literally do anything and it won't drive you insane, toss schoolbuses over ravines, re-enact all the cooking scenes from the Hannibal TV series, not pay for WinRAR even after the free trial period has expired, whatever fiendish machinations you can imagine are yours to vicariously live out through your unstoppable mythic god-monster. On the other hand, I bet Hard Leverage isn't the only wonky interaction that comes from being actually unable to suffer breaking points. Also you probably have to socialize with people who also have absolute freedom from psychospiritual accountability or whatever exactly you consider Integrity to be, so if you have a button there's a chance the horror next door gets a kick out of pushing it. (Although you CAN just eat them)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure Beasts can use mundane Hard Leverage, it just affects them differently, namely by not actually forcing a Breaking Point test, but potentially by modifying a Feeding Test, provided the act lines up with the Beast's Hunger in some way, much the way mundane characters are meant to compare their chosen act to a general set of traumatic experiences, exemplified by the chart on pg. 73. The risk, unlike that of other splats, becomes that you get too far from where you want your Satiety to be, and you either get Anathema'd or your Horror Slumbers and your powers turn off. As for the Socialization thing, mundane humans are probably going to eventually pick up that you aren't exactly right in the head by popular standards, while other supes are either going to be drawn toward or repulsed by your power. You aren't exactly going to be in danger of being hunted down by other Supes, either as a Ridden or a Reaper, although mistakes are bound to happen, but most of the risk is handled by the Hero alerting/triggering mechanics. It's the difference between being immoral versus being amoral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T13:27:04-08:00","id":810784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=810663#post810663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spending willpower is not entirely internal. It represents the character pushing themselves in a time of crisis, and therefore represents them doing something slightly different to someone who didn't spend it. You can't do extra damage to someone just by wishing hard enough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, so, same deal for Hard Leverage. Forcing yourself to shoot someone in the leg is slightly different for a pediatric surgeon than for a career mercenary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T14:04:42-08:00","id":810806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=810784#post810784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Okay, so, same deal for Hard Leverage. Forcing yourself to shoot someone in the leg is slightly different for a pediatric surgeon than for a career mercenary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Those pediatric surgeons leap at the chance to finally let off some of that stress with some quality violence, while the career mercenaries are always careful with their actions, as they'll inevitably face the consequences of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sorry, I had to. In all seriousness with regards to the current argument, Beasts are definitely capable of using Hard Leverage for Social Maneuvering, even if they don't face breaking points. Looming Presence opens an extra Door when using Hard Leverage successfully, and Alien Allure only gives the Charmed Condition if the Beast avoids using Hard Leverage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T09:34:20-08:00","id":811165,"title":"","content":"I've always House ruled it that the Hard Leverage must force a Breaking Point according to the <i>target's </i>standards. Doing something you, personally, find deplorable isn't likely to shake the Werewolf unless it applies to Harmony. I think I remember having this conversation with a friend about Mummy a while back, because a Mummy risking losing Memory over torturous interrogation is kind of funny, because after the first failed roll, they'd be wondering what in Duat they're doing in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T13:45:41-08:00","id":811303,"title":"","content":"That and I think the number of Doors remaining should be a minimum threshold of success for forcing Doors, so Hard Leverage has value and forcing Doors isn't so tempting an option. Because as noted, Beasts are clearly meant to be able to use Hard Leverage - there are references to them doing so - but there isn't really any way I can see for them to actually do it without an Integrity-esque stat that comes with breaking points. Using the target's concept of breaking points makes way more sense than how it works presently, and allows Beasts to use the system as intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T14:43:59-08:00","id":811333,"title":"","content":"How did a &quot;sell me on...&quot; thread become a mechanics discussion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T14:55:19-08:00","id":811339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811333#post811333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did a &quot;sell me on...&quot; thread become a mechanics discussion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cascading failure of situational awareness. Got a pitch to get it back on track?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T15:47:15-08:00","id":811355,"title":"","content":"For me, the biggest obstacle is also one of the biggest draws for me to Beast-the Hungers.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, let's be honest-your initial impression of them is always going to be bad. How else do you respond to the fact that the game asks you to constantly trump other people, to destroy property and lives, to be a miser and a judge? It's dark stuff. It was a big hang-up for me when I started playtesting it.<br /> <br /> But then I started thinking about it in relation to the primordial nature of the protagonists. At the cores of the Hungers are ideas that aren't evil so much as base, and in fact they relate to the old survival needs. Even today, we fight against others to get jobs, collecting money from others so we can grab food at the market before others can snatch them up, making micro-judgments of who to keep in our circles and who not to, and we tear apart old rooms to make room for new people. We as people haven't really evolved that far away from our paleolithic cousins, as far as the essentials go, and it's the ways we <i>have</i> changed that make for compelling narratives and hopes. We as a species will always have ties to our hunter-gatherer days until we completely shed our humanity, if we ever do, and Beast is a great way to look at that-and realize that maybe, that's not necessarily a bad thing, because we've found lots of ways to grow up around our basic instincts and create something more from them.<br /> <br /> And that leads into one of the coolest characters aspects of Beast-subverting and justifying the Hungers. Yes, you hunger for Power, but will you chase wisdom and compassion to become a good 'tyrant'? Who will you seek to gain power over? Yes, you hunger for Prey, but who deserves to be run down, how much do they deserve to know their flesh versus death? So on and so forth.<br /> <br /> Beast is a great game for a lot of reasons-I really do love it as a crossover game-but on it's own merits, Beast is a great game for exploring the whole of ourselves with, by making us confront our basic carnal instincts, good and bad, and explore when, where, how, and why to give them their due, and when too much is too much. It continues the really awesome humanist bent of the Chronicles of Darkness that way.<br /> <br /> Everyone's hungry. How do we justify how we eat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T19:20:20-08:00","id":811467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811165#post811165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always House ruled it that the Hard Leverage must force a Breaking Point according to the <i>target's </i>standards. Doing something you, personally, find deplorable isn't likely to shake the Werewolf unless it applies to Harmony. I think I remember having this conversation with a friend about Mummy a while back, because a Mummy risking losing Memory over torturous interrogation is kind of funny, because after the first failed roll, they'd be wondering what in Duat they're doing in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you get what the Memory mechanic represents. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811303#post811303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That and I think the number of Doors remaining should be a minimum threshold of success for forcing Doors, so Hard Leverage has value and forcing Doors isn't so tempting an option. Because as noted, Beasts are clearly meant to be able to use Hard Leverage - there are references to them doing so - but there isn't really any way I can see for them to actually do it without an Integrity-esque stat that comes with breaking points. Using the target's concept of breaking points makes way more sense than how it works presently, and allows Beasts to use the system as intended.</div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>There is. It's called Feeding. Suffering a Breaking Point is incidental to the end effect.</li> <li>Consulting the Breaking Point table has nothing to do with what the subject is experiencing and everything to do with how convincing the act is.</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 01-18-2016, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T22:47:17-08:00","id":811567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811339#post811339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cascading failure of situational awareness. Got a pitch to get it back on track?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Beast: the Primordial castes you as a human who dreams deep and deeper, down to the primordial fears of humanity. Your whole life is plagued by a particular nightmare and an overwhelming sense that you don't fit in your own skin. One day the monster from your dreams catches you, and you make a choice--embrace the fear and don't wake up. In the afterglow of your own psyche you learn the truth: you have caught you. You are devoured by your truth self and, thereby, come home to the Dark Mother. Now you stalk the world as one of humanity's oldest fears made flesh, and you are Hungry.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 01-19-2016, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T00:23:08-08:00","id":811590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811567#post811567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast: the Primordial. You as a human who dreams deep and deeper, down to the primordial fears of humanity. Plagued by nightmares your whole life, one day your monster catches you and you don't wake up. You learn the truth: you have caught you. You are devoured by your truth self and, thereby, come home to the Dark Mother. Now you embody one of those primal fears and primal Hungers of humanity and, thereby, teach humanity the wisdom it needs to survive in a World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct me if I'm wrong, but that's primarily the first edition of Beast, the kickstarter setting. Though I've heard that some Beasts consider themselves as having had Horrors for souls all along, if it isn't the truth, many have their soul devoured by their new Horror under the guidance of another Beast. I find it's an interesting dynamic to becoming a supernatural, since in most other cases it's involuntary. Vampires may sire you without your consent; werewolves are born as they are; mages awaken simply awaken by accident, and try to awaken others; hunters are recruited or frightened into taking the vigil; prometheans don't have a choice in being created or not; changelings are outright victims and refugees of the Gentry; Sin Eaters have the choice of coming back or continue to<i> die</i>; and demons fall because they can't stay as angels of the God Machine.<br /> <br /> Save for possibly Hunters, Beasts are by and large the ones with the most choice in becoming what they are, because they have to <i>accept</i> the Horror into themselves before it comes to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T01:18:42-08:00","id":811602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811590#post811590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Save for possibly Hunters, Beasts are by and large the ones with the most choice in becoming what they are, because they have to <i>accept</i> the Horror into themselves before it comes to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is partially why I don't like it, because you're making a choice to act as a spirit of cruelty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T01:23:56-08:00","id":811605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811602#post811602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is partially why I don't like it, because you're making a choice to act as a spirit of cruelty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not remotely what the thread is for, Reshy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T05:25:15-08:00","id":811700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811602#post811602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is partially why I don't like it, because you're making a choice to act as a spirit of cruelty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that depends entirely on how you write the character and/or the game. I mean, to look at an example, Hellboy is the Prince of Hell and he's still a good guy. If the Prince of Hell can be a good guy someone that has the spirit of a Kraken/dragon/whatever can be too. You're allowed to change the game around with your ST to fit the character you want to play, that's the beauty of RPGs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T05:32:57-08:00","id":811705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811590#post811590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct me if I'm wrong, but that's primarily the first edition of Beast, the kickstarter setting. Though I've heard that some Beasts consider themselves as having had Horrors for souls all along, if it isn't the truth, many have their soul devoured by their new Horror under the guidance of another Beast. I find it's an interesting dynamic to becoming a supernatural, since in most other cases it's involuntary. Vampires may sire you without your consent; werewolves are born as they are; mages awaken simply awaken by accident, and try to awaken others; hunters are recruited or frightened into taking the vigil; prometheans don't have a choice in being created or not; changelings are outright victims and refugees of the Gentry; Sin Eaters have the choice of coming back or continue to<i> die</i>; and demons fall because they can't stay as angels of the God Machine.<br /> <br /> Save for possibly Hunters, Beasts are by and large the ones with the most choice in becoming what they are, because they have to <i>accept</i> the Horror into themselves before it comes to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the spirit of the writing outside of the introduction* still largely supports the notion that the Horror is the Beast's true self and effectively has always been a part of them, regardless of the involvement of another Begotten, and that Devouring by a second party is a gesture that enables an inevitability rather than birth kin on its own. There is ambiguity in the matter of 'when' and 'how' things change (if they change at all) for the nascent Beast's soul, but the difference is for the most part academic. The one who would become a Beast has always been special by way of their deep connection to the Primordial Dream, and whether that link existed from birth (biological or of the self) or formed at an early period in their life by digging into something that already existed is inconsequential.<br /> <br /> There <i>is</i> an interesting conundrum in that when the Beast can no longer hide behind the crumbling substance of humanity in their soul, they may refuse to accept what they come face to face to. They have a choice, even if they don't understand everything about it. But I imagine that it is like denying that blood runs in your veins, like refusing a natural impulse or inherent feature of your being, and that it must have... interesting consequences.<br /> <br /> *Which they said they would likely go over <i>again</i> once they were done with the text revisions, and since the backer copy also currently has the original chapter 6 and not the revised version I think it's fair to expect a rewritten intro for the final pdf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 01-19-2016, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T05:35:12-08:00","id":811708,"title":"","content":"Is it written anywhere that a Beast automatically enjoys sating it's hunger? If not, isn't it possible for said character to feed, out of necessity, yet, feel nauseated by their own actions? I think that's worth exploring in a character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T05:39:37-08:00","id":811715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811708#post811708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it written anywhere that a Beast automatically enjoys sating it's hunger? If not, isn't it possible for said character to feed, out of necessity, yet, feel nauseated by their own actions? I think that's worth exploring in a character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely agree with this. I think many character fighting with the hunger that they have to sate is great fodder for drama.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T05:42:03-08:00","id":811716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lilappleblossom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811700#post811700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that depends entirely on how you write the character and/or the game. I mean, to look at an example, Hellboy is the Prince of Hell and he's still a good guy. If the Prince of Hell can be a good guy someone that has the spirit of a Kraken/dragon/whatever can be too. You're allowed to change the game around with your ST to fit the character you want to play, that's the beauty of RPGs.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may build on this, Hellboy and Abe are the first examples that came to my mind when thinking about the struggles of a Beast. Being able to rip your horns off and yell &quot;Screw this and the destiny I was born to follow: I'm not going to be as the world expects to be&quot; or at least a &quot;That's what I am and it's not nice, but each day I try to keep going and make the best out of it while aiming to be a decent person, considering the circumstances&quot; are the sorts of character arc I tend to appreciate. Not always, and variety sure is nice, so I don't say you have to play all your Beast characters that way (I would not do so with mine either), but the game still lends itself pretty easily to tell such stories. <br /> <br /> Now that you made me notice this, I guess that explains why I love both Hellboy and Beast","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T05:43:28-08:00","id":811717,"title":"","content":"@Ephsy: Where do you make the separation between the Horror and the Beast? Because the former certainly revels in feasting, and salivates in anticipation of what is to come, and to a degree the Beast consciously shares and partakes of these pangs. There absolutely can be conflict in actions driven by Hunger and the sensations filling it invokes though, and I think it can be both rich and nuanced if it's well played.<br /> <br /> (It occurs to me Kirei Kotomine may be a good study case for that sort of struggle in a Beast. Particularly his character in Fate/Zero. It's not a perfect fit, but the point of the exercise is to draw on it as inspiration by analyzing the parallels, not just port it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T05:45:57-08:00","id":811721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811717#post811717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Ephsy: Where do you make the separation between the Horror and the Beast? Because the former certainly revels in feasting, and salivates in anticipation of what is to come, and to a degree the Beast consciously shares and partakes of these pangs. There absolutely can be conflict in actions driven by Hunger and the sensations filling it invokes though, and I think it can be both rich and nuanced if it's well played.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think of it as a separation between the id and the superego.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T05:52:57-08:00","id":811725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811721#post811721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Think of it as a separation between the id and the superego.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I was getting at was &quot;if the Beast's Id enjoys feeding their Hunger, does the <i>Beast</i> not enjoy it?&quot; Which is not to say there can't be contrary or negative feelings about the act in the ego or superego. There is a natural division of intellectual and instinctual ruminations on its necessity and nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 01-19-2016, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T06:07:14-08:00","id":811734,"title":"","content":"That'd turn into a semantic argument, but I see your point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T06:36:03-08:00","id":811738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lilappleblossom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811700#post811700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that depends entirely on how you write the character and/or the game. I mean, to look at an example, Hellboy is the Prince of Hell and he's still a good guy. If the Prince of Hell can be a good guy someone that has the spirit of a Kraken/dragon/whatever can be too. You're allowed to change the game around with your ST to fit the character you want to play, that's the beauty of RPGs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This really isn't the same kind of thing. Beasts lack anything akin to a morality stat, and not only lack one but what replaces it is a need to inflict cruelty and destroy lives (the exact opposite). I do not believe that is comparable, as last I check Hell Boy didn't need to nearly kill people on a daily basis for a &quot;fix.&quot; Being a Beast a mandate to hurt people, you choose to carry out this mandate and justify it by saying you will choose who &quot;deserves it.&quot; It's all kinds of awful. Being a Beast is the one thing you have the most control over, and then you complain about being given a raw deal?<br /> <br /> I saw someone recommend before that the Heroes should create the Beast, and I felt that made the story dynamic much more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T06:51:26-08:00","id":811751,"title":"","content":"Last time <i>I</i> checked <i>beasts</i> didn't need to nearly kill people on a daily basis for a &quot;fix&quot; either. And if you think they do you really need to go back and re-read the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T06:53:08-08:00","id":811754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811738#post811738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This really isn't the same kind of thing. Beasts lack anything akin to a morality stat, and not only lack one but what replaces it is a need to inflict cruelty and destroy lives (the exact opposite). I do not believe that is comparable, as last I check Hell Boy didn't need to nearly kill people on a daily basis for a &quot;fix.&quot; Being a Beast a mandate to hurt people, you choose to carry out this mandate and justify it by saying you will choose who &quot;deserves it.&quot; It's all kinds of awful. Being a Beast is the one thing you have the most control over, and then you complain about being given a raw deal?<br /> <br /> I saw someone recommend before that the Heroes should create the Beast, and I felt that made the story dynamic much more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making the &quot;choice&quot; to be a Beast is usually done during times of stress, and most proto-Beasts feel like it will be an answer to the question &quot;Who am I?&quot; that's been plaguing them for their whole lives. It's a classic deal with the devil, though in this case the devil is yourself and there's no way to renege.<br /> <br /> Or, more simply, they don't have all of the relevant details before they accept what they are. There's no contract with fine print that they can go over first. I bet most Begotten who assist proto-Beasts probably leave out those details as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T07:00:00-08:00","id":811763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811751#post811751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last time <i>I</i> checked <i>beasts</i> didn't need to nearly kill people on a daily basis for a &quot;fix&quot; either. And if you think they do you really need to go back and re-read the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the Hunger. However, all of the hungers involve traumatizing people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811754#post811754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Making the &quot;choice&quot; to be a Beast is usually done during times of stress, and most proto-Beasts feel like it will be an answer to the question &quot;Who am I?&quot; that's been plaguing them for their whole lives. It's a classic deal with the devil, though in this case the devil is yourself and there's no way to renege.<br /> <br /> Or, more simply, they don't have all of the relevant details before they accept what they are. There's no contract with fine print that they can go over first. I bet most Begotten who assist proto-Beasts probably leave out those details as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, why should the people around you suffer trauma because <b>you</b> made a mistake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T07:07:57-08:00","id":811767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811763#post811763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still, why should the people around you suffer trauma because <b>you</b> made a mistake?</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured that question was the heart of the Personal Horror aspect of Beast. That you don't like it explains much about why you don't like the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T07:08:27-08:00","id":811768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811738#post811738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This really isn't the same kind of thing. Beasts lack anything akin to a morality stat, and not only lack one but what replaces it is a need to inflict cruelty and destroy lives (the exact opposite). I do not believe that is comparable, as last I check Hell Boy didn't need to nearly kill people on a daily basis for a &quot;fix.&quot; Being a Beast a mandate to hurt people, you choose to carry out this mandate and justify it by saying you will choose who &quot;deserves it.&quot; It's all kinds of awful. Being a Beast is the one thing you have the most control over, and then you complain about being given a raw deal?<br /> <br /> I saw someone recommend before that the Heroes should create the Beast, and I felt that made the story dynamic much more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who cares if there's no stat? Now we're getting into an argument of rules vs. narrative. Your character can have as much morality as you want. If you want a morality stat you can always houserule one. I feel like it's bit of a nitpick in this case. You don't always have to follow the rules exactly as written if you don't find that fun. You can also just not buy the system if it's not something you're interested in. So far all of the complaints you've given sound like more of a matter of taste than honest critique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T07:44:52-08:00","id":811794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811738#post811738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This really isn't the same kind of thing. Beasts lack anything akin to a morality stat, and not only lack one but what replaces it is a need to inflict cruelty and destroy lives (the exact opposite). I do not believe that is comparable, as last I check Hell Boy didn't need to nearly kill people on a daily basis for a &quot;fix.&quot; Being a Beast a mandate to hurt people...</div> </div> </div> </div>Being Hellboy is a mandate to be the herald of the Apocalypse, inheritor of Satan's throne, leader of the Infernal Armies that will topple Heaven and, just to add more, key to the release of the absolute worst evils of his setting, entities that see the corruption and extermination of the whole mankind as trivial but enjoyable matters. I'd say he qualifies. He was <i>made </i> with the purpose to inflict cruelty and destroy lives and if you think that he has not to fight with his nature daily, well, I can only think you're talking about the movies because in the comics it practically happens every single time nowadays<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811738#post811738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you choose to carry out this mandate and justify it by saying you will choose who &quot;deserves it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Is that mandatory? I mean, this method of dealing with dark urges has an old and honored tradition in media but it's far, far, from being the only way a Beast can handle and relate to her Hunger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811763#post811763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still, why should the people around you suffer trauma because <b>you</b> made a mistake?</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking in absolutes outside of character? That's a tricky territory but if I have to give an answer I'd say they shouldn't. And that's kinda the point, how do you balance your nature, which is under many aspects unsavory to the daily well-being of other individuals, and your own morality. Impulse against thought, hoping to not mess up too much","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-19-2016, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:24:35-08:00","id":811820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811794#post811794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's kinda the point, how do you balance your nature, which is under many aspects unsavory to the daily well-being of other individuals, and your own morality. Impulse against thought, hoping to not mess up too much</div> </div> </div> </div>That monologue Jules Winnfield gives at the end of Pulp Fiction rather nicely sums up why I find the notion that the &quot;try to let them learn something from it&quot; aspect of Beast culture is <i>just</i> a rationalization to be kind of ill-conceived; it's pretty plain that that's a model of activity that is at least making an attempt at civic responsibility.<br /> <br /> It's a model that says Mister Nine-Millimeter is not the shepherd, and I think that's pretty damn important to remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:29:46-08:00","id":811826,"title":"","content":"IIRC the current version has the teaching thing be Beasts trying to pick up the slack on something they're not really built to do. The <i>heroes</i> are supposed to be the teachers. The Beasts are supposed to be the cautionary tale itself or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:59:51-08:00","id":811848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lilappleblossom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811715#post811715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely agree with this. I think many character fighting with the hunger that they have to sate is great fodder for drama.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I've maintained that Beast is a game about addiction. The lack of set in stone moral imperatives allows you to be as dark a shade of gray as you need in pursuit of indulging or denying that urge, even if that grey, in the long run, turns out to be as pure white as driven snow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 01-19-2016, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T11:38:38-08:00","id":811973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811738#post811738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This really isn't the same kind of thing. Beasts lack anything akin to a morality stat, and not only lack one but what replaces it is a need to inflict cruelty and destroy lives (the exact opposite). I do not believe that is comparable, as last I check Hell Boy didn't need to nearly kill people on a daily basis for a &quot;fix.&quot; Being a Beast a mandate to hurt people, you choose to carry out this mandate and justify it by saying you will choose who &quot;deserves it.&quot; It's all kinds of awful. Being a Beast is the one thing you have the most control over, and then you complain about being given a raw deal?<br /> <br /> I saw someone recommend before that the Heroes should create the Beast, and I felt that made the story dynamic much more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has been explained elsewhere better, but Beasts do have something of a morality stat Reshy; Satiety. The more sated a Beast is, the more like themselves they think, because their Horror is sated and isn't thinking about frightening others to feed itself, whereas the hungrier the Horror is, the more the Beast looks to others for food. It's an interesting dichotomy in the game, and something that the developers have also discussed - do you become someone who hunts only when they need to, driving your thoughts more feral and risk starving their inner Horror, or do you make peace with your nature and more regularly hunt to keep yourself as <i>you</i> and your Horror satisfied?<br /> <br /> As noted elsewhere, again, this ties into the overall theme of (at least the early) World of Darkness gamelines - be monsters so you do not become <i>monsters</i>. A sated Horror is less likely to drive someone to really hurt another when sated than one that is starving - keep your thoughts clear and you're able to keep things better under control, and more likely to have some good come out of it. Again, as noted elsewhere (it bugs me I don't have citations for this) plenty of the horrors of Beast stem from every day fears that Beasts simply employ to their own ends. They're fears we don't want, yes, but having a fear of going into an alleyway alone or of going to a new place of dubious quality are ones that society beat into us simply because, well, it's a way to keep people safe. It's a guidance, fear, and if you understand it you can use it to help keep others safe. Scare them away from a drug habit, keep an abusive family member in line, make thieves reconsider breaking and entering, or even something as mundane as making someone be pleasant to the world. It's a similar tactic to what parents do to keep their children growing up right. Heck, if you're really good about it you could even make it into something like &quot;A Christmas Carol&quot;, scaring someone about where their life is going to get them to really rethink their lives.<br /> <br /> It's not a marker for overall Morality, of course, but a personal one; a grandmother and a serial killer can both have a Satiety of 9 regularly, but the true morality of them is how they get there. Satiety just marks how much of their morals are actually theirs and how much of it is hunger.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's not to say that all Beasts will consider doing this, just as you can't assume everyone will return a good deed or favor done for them. That's just people, and (again) as noted elsewhere, sometimes normal people can be as much monsters as the playable Splats can be. Just look at, say, Hunter.<br /> <br /> That's also not taking advantage of the many ways a Beast can get Satiety without hurting one person <i>at all</i>. Given the extended family Beasts have, suffice to say, <i>they have options</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 01-19-2016, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T12:02:09-08:00","id":811994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=807900#post807900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beast as a whole is very interesting, I would say consider it as a book for antagonists for your games that you run. Beasts have the power to make other supernaturals inherently like them, somehow. This makes them all very well connected as supernaturals are predisposed to like the creature of living nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No. No, they don't. This is one of the most common misconceptions about <b>Beast</b> and I'd kind of like it to die in a fire. Beasts, <i>all else being equal</i>, start with a good first impression. That's all it means. Other supernatural creatures are inclined to give them the benefit of the doubt. That's it. A foot in the door. Beasts can fuck that right into the ground if they act like jerks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T12:07:44-08:00","id":811997,"title":"","content":"Reshy, you aren't interested in selling Beast, warts and all. You're turning this into a platform to bitch about Beast. It's not welcome or appreciated anymore. You gave your opinion, that was cool, and now you're harping, that's not.<br /> <br /> Clear off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:06:55-08:00","id":812045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811339#post811339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cascading failure of situational awareness. Got a pitch to get it back on track?</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast: the Primordial </b>gives you an opportunity to do something amazing and evocative heretofore only touched upon by other gamelines, and that is the power to build your own psychic nightmare dungeon where you can literally go hang out with your friends. Beasts have lots of awesome debuff powers, a selection of the coolest things you can get in other lines - flight, regeneration, insane Brawl-based aggravated damage, invisibility, mind control/social domination powers - and are open both in terms of personal character development and in terms of crossover potential, although I can't honestly say that will always be an easy sell, given their power and focuses. You can do, ST willing, basically whatever you want with them. They have no leaders to pass law, no organizations to curtail behavior, and no real INTERNAL pressures - they are also the first to be truly and utterly amoral. Any system or code of behavior you devise works with Beast so long as it doesn't including starving to 0 Satiety. They're ridiculously customizable. And that includes the psychic nightmare dungeons.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> On the topical subject of how evil you have to be - where the answer to how evil CAN you be is &quot;think of the worst thing you can think of one superhuman entity doing to a defenseless human being, you can use that to satisfy Hunger and it can't even ping your nonexistent karma meter&quot; - the answer is &quot;really not that terrible.&quot; You can be an Eshmaki who sneaks into the cabins at the Girl Scout retreat with a shotgun and just...stands there for a moment, and then goes home. You can have invisibility magic so there's not even really any danger of being seen. That works. Now, you're (I think this holds true in the backer version) not making the choice on what's okay IC, that's on your Horror to decide, but you as a player can pick something with a really low impact. Steal things that can't be replaced but maybe aren't MISSED too terribly much. Create a software company where everyone's kinda scared of you but proud of the work they do, with the pride outweighing the fear, that's not so bad. Demolish condemned buildings after checking for the homeless. You can skip the priest-killing home-invading PTSD-inflicting bone-breaking stuff, and if you meet another Beast who DOESN'T skip it, you can murder her with a clean conscience.<br /> <br /> So there's another point for the customization angle, you can actually be pretty low on the wickedness scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","user":"Kingdom of One","date":". 01-19-2016, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:25:57-08:00","id":812059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811602#post811602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is partially why I don't like it, because you're making a choice to act as a spirit of cruelty.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#ff0000\">\u200bThe title of the thread is &quot;Sell me Beast&quot; not &quot;List reasons why I don't like Beast&quot;. Please stay on topic/don't thread crap. Thanks.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:49:22-08:00","id":812080,"title":"","content":"Btw, does anyone know when Beast is coming out on drivethru? Can't find it anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:58:11-08:00","id":812091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=812080#post812080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, does anyone know when Beast is coming out on drivethru? Can't find it anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>It shouldn't be terribly long. The core book is currently listed as being in &quot;Indexing&quot; in the most recent update, and has steadily progressed through the previous ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/post-milwaukee-dizziness-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/post-milwaukee-dizziness-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\"> Post-Milwaukee Dizziness [Monday Meeting Notes] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/post-milwaukee-dizziness-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/post-milwaukee-dizziness-monday-meeting-notes/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'd give it a month, maybe two at most, but I really don't know what Indexing entails, nor how long it generally takes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T10:38:01-08:00","id":812710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=811708#post811708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it written anywhere that a Beast automatically enjoys sating it's hunger? If not, isn't it possible for said character to feed, out of necessity, yet, feel nauseated by their own actions? I think that's worth exploring in a character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given their nature and connection to the Horror, I think they're very likely to enjoy it on a biological level - but they may not like <i>that</i> they enjoy it, or consider enjoying it a good enough reason to do it cavalierly. (Cf how Buffy feels about killing).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T10:46:40-08:00","id":812717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=812710#post812710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given their nature and connection to the Horror, I think they're very likely to enjoy it on a biological level - but they may not like <i>that</i> they enjoy it, or consider enjoying it a good enough reason to do it cavalierly. (Cf how Buffy feels about killing).</div> </div> </div> </div>It might cause a kind of dissonance between the Mind of the Beast which knows it shouldn't enjoy it and the Body/Soul of the Beast which definitely enjoys it. I'd imagine it'd feel almost akin to having sex, since that's also (consequently) how Beasts &quot;reproduce.&quot; <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:36:42-08:00","id":812758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=812717#post812717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd imagine it'd feel almost akin to having sex, since that's also (consequently) how Beasts &quot;reproduce.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearing a plot of land so that the existing seed of a terrifying mandragora-cactus can grow on it isn't what I'd call analogous to fertilization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:32:07-08:00","id":812787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/806974-sell-me-beast?p=812717#post812717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It might cause a kind of dissonance between the Mind of the Beast which knows it shouldn't enjoy it and the Body/Soul of the Beast which definitely enjoys it. I'd imagine it'd feel almost akin to having sex, since that's also (consequently) how Beasts &quot;reproduce.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really I mean nothing in the book has indicated feeding as part of the process for making new Beasts aside from the obvious bit where starving to death is counterproductive to reproduction. (Though I think that's true for anything that isn't a mayfly.) I mean the Devouring has a fair amount of questions around it like whether or not its your own Horror that does it or someone else's Horror.<br /> <br /> As far as Epshy's question on whether or not a Beast automatically enjoys sating its Hunger goes; I think there is at least a little satisfaction from it by default. I mean the book does state that the Horror gives no craps about anything beyond feeding, so as long as its eating it'll be happy and since it is a part of the whole there will be at least a little satisfaction carried over to the human part of the mind even if the actions done to facilitate the feeding would normally repulse the person.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T13:25:13-08:00","id":812853,"title":"","content":"Clearly anyone who's done the walk of shame understands how you may enjoy doing something but then... you don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}